review.notes:
All 10 nodes and all links were checked against the library copies of Scholze, p-adic Hodge theory for rigid-analytic varieties (author version of 3 Nov 2012, SHA-256 verified; line numbers of the library text extraction reproduce), and the 3-page erratum (SHA-256 verified). The reviewer additionally read Proposition 3.15, Lemma 3.16, Corollary 3.17, Definition 5.9, Lemma 5.10 and the bibliography, and Sch12 Theorem 6.3 in a regenerated layout extraction. All 10 nodes were corrected; none was unverifiable. Main corrections:
(1) Remark 6.20's general formula was copied with a printed misprint (Ω^i log χ for i = j + 1; the formula derivable from Proposition 6.16 has Ω^j log χ).
(2) An acceptance test asserted that Ô_X^+(X) is the p-adic completion of O^+(X) for affinoid X, which the source explicitly says is not known in general.
(3) The ξ construction needs x_i ∈ K♭+, not O_{K♭}.
(4) Definition 5.9 was misdescribed, Proposition 6.7's base was misstated, and the Lemma 6.11 hypothesis (K, O_K) was dropped.
(5) Packet-authored proof expansions (Poincaré lemma, R^1 lim, Γ_k-descent) are now labelled, and asserted steps are listed.
Links:
(a) the Sch12 Theorem 6.3(ii) supplier was re-pointed from P2/sheaf-theorem to P2/tilting-homeomorphism-and-rational-subsets;
(b) the Definition 4.1 link was re-targeted from the affinoid-perfectoid node (which does not use it) to the Lemma 4.10 node;
(c) three links were added: P1/fontaine-theta and P1/tilt-of-perfectoid-tate-ring → R06.1 node, and R06.1 node → local-structure node (Corollary 6.4 in Lemma 6.11);
(d) the AI.0:integral → R06.1 link is annotated as an atlas compatibility constraint, since AI.0:integral covers only (C, O_C);
(e) the CP.3 export is annotated because its consumer use site is unread;
(f) the Theorem 6.5, OB_dR, Poincaré-lemma and Section 6.16 link reasons were sharpened.
All parentStageIds (R06.1, P8:local-rational) are owned by PadicHodgeTheory. All 10 coverage stage ids exist; the P7 record was not a container and now lists its real scope. Three gaps were added. Packet status stays partial.
